g2004/long-wind","Game source, shaders, textures, GLB characters and animations are included. Tripo and Mixamo assets have separate terms; see CREDITS.md.","Access type","playable","demo","Play or run",[128],{"_65":129,"_31":130,"_113":131},"Play Long Wind","https://jbang2004.github.io/long-wind/","WASD moves, mouse attacks/guards, Space dodges, Q locks on. Touch controls support landscape play.","Game platform","Browser","Guide format","build log","tutorial","Build story / tutorial",[139],{"_65":140,"_31":112,"_113":-7},"Read the creator’s development timeline","Study this workflow","ordered",true,[145,146,147,148],"Try movement, guarding, dodging, and the opening boss.","Read the Chinese development account and human contribution disclosure.","Study the contracts, art bible, and animation pipeline.","Check CREDITS.md before adapting included assets.","AI workflow / foundation context","The author describes directing Claude Code in Chinese, playtesting its changes, and supplying Tripo and Mixamo access. The README includes a development timeline.","aiUse","guidance","Creation category","AI-assisted (creator attribution)","category","provenance","Track","3D","track","metadata","Asset creation tools",false,[165,166],"assetTools","Tripo","Adobe Mixamo","Engine","Three.js · JavaScript","engine","lead","3d","ai-assisted",[165,166],[145,146,147,148],{"_65":140,"_31":112,"_23":185},{"_65":129,"_31":130,"_23":124,"_113":131},{"_65":120,"_31":121,"_183":184,"_113":122},{"_65":111,"_31":112,"_113":114},[180,181,182],"claude-code","threejs","blender","scope","complete-project","build-log","example:sprout-quest-claude","sprout-quest-claude","Sprout Quest","Explore a small world, fight real-time arena battles, gather materials, craft gear and rebuild a village. Sprout Quest is a mobile-first adventure with a 2D world and live-rendered 3D characters and items.","/examples/sprout-quest-claude/",{"_25":187,"_27":188,"_29":189,"_169":253,"_164":254,"_159":255,"_155":256,"_151":249,"_9":257,"_136":258,"_125":259,"_38":260,"_109":261,"_97":262},[193,194,195,196,197,198,199,200,201,202,203,204,205,206,207,208,209,210,211,212,213],{"_61":27,"_74":188,"_63":27,"_98":-7},{"_61":170,"_74":189,"_63":29,"_98":-7},{"_61":71,"_65":167,"_74":253,"_63":169,"_98":152},{"_61":90,"_65":161,"_142":162,"_67":252,"_63":164,"_98":-7},{"_61":71,"_65":157,"_74":251,"_63":159,"_98":160},{"_61":71,"_65":153,"_74":250,"_63":155,"_98":156},{"_61":71,"_65":149,"_74":249,"_63":151,"_98":152},{"_61":90,"_65":141,"_142":143,"_67":244,"_63":9,"_98":-7},{"_61":62,"_65":137,"_67":241,"_63":136,"_98":-7},{"_61":71,"_65":134,"_74":135,"_63":136,"_98":-7},{"_61":71,"_65":132,"_74":133,"_63":125,"_98":-7},{"_61":62,"_65":126,"_67":236,"_63":125,"_98":-7},{"_61":71,"_65":123,"_74":124,"_63":125,"_98":-7},{"_61":62,"_65":117,"_67":232,"_63":38,"_98":-7},{"_61":71,"_65":115,"_74":116,"_63":38,"_98":-7},{"_61":62,"_65":107,"_67":227,"_63":109,"_98":-7},{"_61":62,"_65":95,"_67":223,"_63":97,"_98":-7},{"_61":90,"_63":91,"_65":92,"_67":222},{"_61":76,"_63":77,"_65":218,"_79":219,"_81":220,"_38":221,"_84":85,"_86":87,"_88":89},{"_61":71,"_63":72,"_65":73,"_74":217},{"_61":62,"_63":64,"_65":66,"_67":214},[215],{"_65":66,"_31":216},"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/aibengineering/sprout-quest/main/docs/teaser.webp","2026-10-20","A combat frame from the creator’s portrait gameplay animation, fitted without cropping.","/GameMap/assets/media/learning/sprout-quest-claude.webp","A small sword-wielding adventurer fights creatures on a forest path, with a portrait mobile touch joystick.","https://github.com/aibengineering/sprout-quest#readme",[94],[224,225,226],{"_65":94,"_31":106},{"_65":104,"_31":105},{"_65":102,"_31":103},[228],{"_65":229,"_31":230,"_113":231},"Read the creator’s AI attribution","https://github.com/aibengineering/sprout-quest#how-it-was-built","README separates the original build from later human playtest/AI iteration; publishes source modules, generated models and runtime assets, plus a prompt summary. Source-checked; full reproduction not performed.",[233],{"_65":120,"_31":234,"_113":235},"https://github.com/aibengineering/sprout-quest","Complete game code, runtime GLBs/sprite atlases, Blender scripts and tests. bun install then bun run dev opens localhost:3000; normal builds use committed art and do not require Blender. No root LICENSE was found, so public source visibility does not establish broad reuse permission.",[237],{"_65":238,"_31":239,"_113":240},"Play Sprout Quest","https://aibengineering.github.io/sprout-quest/","Author-hosted browser adventure designed for portrait phones, with desktop keyboard controls and localStorage saves.",[242],{"_65":243,"_31":230,"_113":-7},"Read the creator’s build account",[245,246,247,248],"Play the portrait-browser prologue and follow its first fight, gathering and forge tasks.","Read the build account to see how human phone playtests guided later Claude Code changes.","Run bun install and bun run dev; inspect the game modules, committed runtime assets and Blender builders.","Change one combat, crafting or story rule with an agent, then replay the affected progression and save flow.","The creator says Claude Code generated the game, tests and Blender art pipeline from plain-language requests while the human played on a phone and gave feedback. The repository contains the runtime art as well as its source builders.","AI-generated (creator attribution)","2D",[102],"Custom Canvas 2D + Three.js · TypeScript",[102],"2d","ai-generated",[245,246,247,248],{"_65":243,"_31":230,"_23":185},{"_65":238,"_31":239,"_23":124,"_113":240},{"_65":120,"_31":234,"_113":235,"_183":184},{"_65":229,"_31":230,"_113":231},[180,181,182],"example:golden-hour-skatepark-cursor","golden-hour-skatepark-cursor","Golden Hour Skatepark","Skate an original beachside park: carve transitions, ollie, flip, grind, manual, bail and recover. This complete third-person sandbox has transient trick combos and a changeable time of day, with no levels or persistent score.","/examples/golden-hour-skatepark-cursor/",{"_25":264,"_27":265,"_29":266,"_169":329,"_164":330,"_159":171,"_155":172,"_151":327,"_9":331,"_136":332,"_125":333,"_38":334,"_109":335,"_97":336},[270,271,272,273,274,275,276,277,278,279,280,281,282,283,284,285,286,287,288,289,290],{"_61":27,"_74":265,"_63":27,"_98":-7},{"_61":170,"_74":266,"_63":29,"_98":-7},{"_61":71,"_65":167,"_74":329,"_63":169,"_98":152},{"_61":90,"_65":161,"_142":162,"_67":328,"_63":164,"_98":-7},{"_61":71,"_65":157,"_74":158,"_63":159,"_98":160},{"_61":71,"_65":153,"_74":154,"_63":155,"_98":156},{"_61":71,"_65":149,"_74":327,"_63":151,"_98":152},{"_61":90,"_65":141,"_142":143,"_67":322,"_63":9,"_98":-7},{"_61":62,"_65":137,"_67":318,"_63":136,"_98":-7},{"_61":71,"_65":134,"_74":135,"_63":136,"_98":-7},{"_61":71,"_65":132,"_74":133,"_63":125,"_98":-7},{"_61":62,"_65":126,"_67":313,"_63":125,"_98":-7},{"_61":71,"_65":123,"_74":124,"_63":125,"_98":-7},{"_61":62,"_65":117,"_67":308,"_63":38,"_98":-7},{"_61":71,"_65":115,"_74":116,"_63":38,"_98":-7},{"_61":62,"_65":107,"_67":303,"_63":109,"_98":-7},{"_61":62,"_65":95,"_67":300,"_63":97,"_98":-7},{"_61":90,"_63":91,"_65":92,"_67":298},{"_61":76,"_63":77,"_65":294,"_79":295,"_81":296,"_38":297,"_84":85,"_86":87,"_88":89},{"_61":71,"_63":72,"_65":73,"_74":217},{"_61":62,"_63":64,"_65":66,"_67":291},[292],{"_65":66,"_31":293},"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/StarKnightt/skate-park/main/docs/media/02-half-pipe-air.jpg","The creator’s actual half-pipe gameplay frame, with the skater and the procedural park.","/GameMap/assets/media/learning/golden-hour-skatepark-cursor.webp","A skater is airborne above a half-pipe in a palm-lined skatepark under a warm evening sky.","https://github.com/StarKnightt/skate-park#readme",[299],"Cursor",[301,302],{"_65":104,"_31":105},{"_65":102,"_31":103},[304],{"_65":305,"_31":306,"_113":307},"Read the creator’s Cursor contribution account","https://github.com/StarKnightt/skate-park#how-it-was-built","The README explicitly names Cursor AI agents and separates builder passes, critic feedback and human playtests; docs/MAKING-OF.md provides a detailed account. Source-checked; performance and playability claims were not reproduced.",[309],{"_65":310,"_31":311,"_113":312},"Open the complete skating project","https://github.com/StarKnightt/skate-park","Complete TypeScript game, procedural park code, runtime skater/crowd GLBs, textures, audio and source tools. CI uses Node 22 and pnpm 10.18.0; pnpm install then pnpm dev at 127.0.0.1:5188. Ports are fixed. No root LICENSE was found; CC0 media, Mixamo animations and dependencies keep separate terms.",[314],{"_65":315,"_31":316,"_113":317},"Play Golden Hour Skatepark","https://starknightt.github.io/skate-park/","Browser skating sandbox with keyboard, optional mouse/gamepad and touch controls. Press any key, click or tap to take over from the title-screen rider. Phone testing reported by the creator used desktop emulation; Firefox and desktop Safari remain untested.",[319],{"_65":320,"_31":321,"_113":-7},"Read the builder-and-critic development account","https://github.com/StarKnightt/skate-park/blob/main/docs/MAKING-OF.md",[323,324,325,326],"Play the park and test pushing, carving, one trick, a bail and recovery.","Read the making-of account and separate human feedback, agent implementation and third-party assets.","Use Node 22 with pnpm 10.18.0, then pnpm install and pnpm dev; inspect the collision mesh and character pipeline.","Ask an agent to adjust one movement or camera parameter, then compare transition riding, tricks and recovery across the park.","The author says Cursor AI agents implemented the game through builder and visual-critic passes, with human playtests refining controls. Code-built environments and procedural riding are combined with Cursor-generated artwork, credited CC0 audio/textures and Mixamo recovery animations.",[102],"Three.js · TypeScript",[102],[323,324,325,326],{"_65":320,"_31":321,"_23":185},{"_65":315,"_31":316,"_23":124,"_113":317},{"_65":310,"_31":311,"_183":184,"_113":312},{"_65":305,"_31":306,"_113":307},[181,182],"example:core-business-claude","core-business-claude","Core Business","Drill for minerals, manage fuel and hull condition, and spend earnings at surface shops in a non-commercial mining tech demo inspired by Motherload. Three.js renders the 2.5D world while Blender scripts produce its 3D assets.","/examples/core-business-claude/",{"_25":338,"_27":339,"_29":340,"_169":168,"_159":171,"_155":172,"_151":396,"_9":399,"_136":400,"_125":401,"_38":402,"_109":403,"_97":404,"_164":405},[344,345,346,347,348,349,350,351,352,353,354,355,356,357,358,359,360,361,362,363],{"_61":27,"_74":339,"_63":27,"_98":-7},{"_61":170,"_74":340,"_63":29,"_98":-7},{"_61":71,"_65":167,"_74":168,"_63":169,"_98":152},{"_61":90,"_65":161,"_142":162,"_67":397,"_63":164,"_98":-7},{"_61":71,"_65":157,"_74":158,"_63":159,"_98":160},{"_61":71,"_65":153,"_74":154,"_63":155,"_98":156},{"_61":71,"_65":149,"_74":396,"_63":151,"_98":152},{"_61":90,"_65":141,"_142":143,"_67":391,"_63":9,"_98":-7},{"_61":62,"_65":137,"_67":388,"_63":136,"_98":-7},{"_61":71,"_65":134,"_74":135,"_63":136,"_98":-7},{"_61":71,"_65":132,"_74":133,"_63":125,"_98":-7},{"_61":62,"_65":126,"_67":384,"_63":125,"_98":-7},{"_61":71,"_65":123,"_74":124,"_63":125,"_98":-7},{"_61":62,"_65":117,"_67":380,"_63":38,"_98":-7},{"_61":71,"_65":115,"_74":116,"_63":38,"_98":-7},{"_61":62,"_65":107,"_67":376,"_63":109,"_98":-7},{"_61":62,"_65":95,"_67":373,"_63":97,"_98":-7},{"_61":90,"_63":91,"_65":92,"_67":371},{"_61":76,"_63":77,"_65":366,"_79":367,"_81":368,"_38":369,"_84":85,"_86":87,"_88":370},{"_61":71,"_63":364,"_65":365,"_74":217},"captureDate","Screenshot captured","The running author-hosted mining tech demo, captured with the Metal rendering backend.","/GameMap/assets/media/learning/core-business-claude.webp","The Core Business mining vehicle in a three-dimensional side-view Mars scene, with fuel, hull, cargo, money and depth indicators.","https://leichtbier.github.io/core-business/","GameMap browser capture",[372],"Claude model / chat",[374,375],{"_65":104,"_31":105},{"_65":102,"_31":103},[377],{"_65":229,"_31":378,"_113":379},"https://github.com/Leichtbier/core-business#readme","The author explicitly separates Claude-generated work from ElevenLabs audio and credits Motherload/XGen Studios. This does not imply that Claude created the original game’s rules.",[381],{"_65":120,"_31":382,"_113":383},"https://github.com/Leichtbier/core-business","Complete JavaScript game, vendored Three.js, committed GLBs, Blender source scripts, UI, audio and tests. Serve the root, e.g. python3 -m http.server 5173; Blender regeneration is unnecessary for normal play. Code is MIT with explicit exceptions: ElevenLabs audio is supplied for this project, not separate extraction or redistribution; see LICENSE.",[385],{"_65":386,"_31":369,"_113":387},"Play Core Business","WebGL browser, keyboard/pointer and touch controls. Initial graphics preparation stalled with the default headless renderer; Chrome with Metal reached normal play. After the opening transmission, brief movement/drilling input produced score 25 and fuel/depth feedback. Full mining progression and audio were not tested.",[389],{"_65":390,"_31":378,"_113":-7},"Read the mining game’s implementation and asset pipeline",[392,393,394,395],"Start a new game and learn movement, downward drilling, fuel and return-to-surface shops.","Read the fixed-step simulation separately from the Three.js renderer and committed GLB models.","Serve the repository root with a static HTTP server; opening ES modules via file:// does not work.","Change one mineral or upgrade rule, then check drilling, selling, fuel use and save/reload.","The creator attributes the game code, tests, textures, translations, models and Blender generation scripts to Claude Opus 5.5. ElevenLabs supplied the sound and music. The project reimplements Motherload-style rules with new assets and explicitly describes itself as a non-commercial experiment; the coding client is not named.",[102,398],"ElevenLabs",[392,393,394,395],{"_65":390,"_31":378,"_23":185},{"_65":386,"_31":369,"_23":124,"_113":387},{"_65":120,"_31":382,"_183":184,"_113":383},{"_65":229,"_31":378,"_113":379},[181,182],[102,398],"example:polar-icecapade-claude","polar-icecapade-claude","Polar Icecapade","Slide across icy 3D arenas, use a three-hit melee combo to propel yourself forward, and fire projectiles that push you backward. Open gates and collect coins while confronting a rat regime in a short game-jam adventure.","/examples/polar-icecapade-claude/",{"_25":407,"_27":408,"_29":409,"_169":470,"_159":171,"_155":172,"_151":466,"_164":471,"_9":472,"_136":473,"_125":474,"_38":475,"_109":476,"_97":477},[413,414,415,416,417,418,419,420,421,422,423,424,425,426,427,428,429,430,431,432],{"_61":27,"_74":408,"_63":27,"_98":-7},{"_61":170,"_74":409,"_63":29,"_98":-7},{"_61":71,"_65":167,"_74":470,"_63":169,"_98":152},{"_61":90,"_65":161,"_142":162,"_67":467,"_63":164,"_98":-7},{"_61":71,"_65":157,"_74":158,"_63":159,"_98":160},{"_61":71,"_65":153,"_74":154,"_63":155,"_98":156},{"_61":71,"_65":149,"_74":466,"_63":151,"_98":152},{"_61":90,"_65":141,"_142":143,"_67":461,"_63":9,"_98":-7},{"_61":62,"_65":137,"_67":458,"_63":136,"_98":-7},{"_61":71,"_65":134,"_74":135,"_63":136,"_98":-7},{"_61":71,"_65":132,"_74":457,"_63":125,"_98":-7},{"_61":62,"_65":126,"_67":453,"_63":125,"_98":-7},{"_61":71,"_65":123,"_74":124,"_63":125,"_98":-7},{"_61":62,"_65":117,"_67":448,"_63":38,"_98":-7},{"_61":71,"_65":115,"_74":116,"_63":38,"_98":-7},{"_61":62,"_65":107,"_67":444,"_63":109,"_98":-7},{"_61":62,"_65":95,"_67":438,"_63":97,"_98":-7},{"_61":90,"_63":91,"_65":92,"_67":437},{"_61":76,"_63":77,"_65":433,"_79":434,"_81":435,"_38":436,"_84":85,"_86":87,"_88":370},{"_61":71,"_63":364,"_65":365,"_74":217},"The live first level after melee movement and a shot; ammo has fallen to 11/12.","/GameMap/assets/media/learning/polar-icecapade-claude.webp","Polar Icecapade’s first icy 3D arena after melee propulsion and a shot, showing the moving character, gates, coins, timer and 11 of 12 ammunition.","https://evankurtzart.itch.io/polar-icecapade",[94],[439,440,441],{"_65":94,"_31":106},{"_65":442,"_31":443},{"_65":102,"_31":103},"Godot Engine · Official Documentation","/resources/godot-engine/",[445],{"_65":446,"_31":436,"_113":447},"Read the team’s explicit Claude Code assistance statement","The creators distinguish AI help with diagnosing and implementing core code from their own code review, modeling, animation and art. The page links the full game source and identifies Godot 4.6 and GDScript; its “No generative AI” content badge does not erase the separate coding-assistance disclosure.",[449],{"_65":450,"_31":451,"_113":452},"Open the complete Godot game project","https://github.com/afenkurtz/Big-Mode-Game-Jam-2026/tree/main/slick","Complete Godot 4.6 project with levels, GDScript, GLB/FBX models, Blender authoring files, textures, UI and audio. The inspected tree has 292 files, about 239 MB. Open the slick folder; importing Blender authoring files may require a compatible Blender installation. No top-level game license was found; external sounds, music and fonts retain their separately credited terms.",[454],{"_65":455,"_31":436,"_113":456},"Play or download Polar Icecapade on itch.io","Mouse recommended: left-click performs melee propulsion, right-click shoots with recoil, and Escape pauses. Browser review reached the first level, moved, fired a projectile with ammo changing from 12 to 11, and opened pause. The roughly 170 MB web build has author-documented performance limits; Windows/Linux downloads are provided and mobile is not recommended. Later levels and a complete run were not tested.","itch.io",[459],{"_65":460,"_31":436,"_113":-7},"Read the team’s development and asset breakdown",[462,463,464,465],"Start the first browser level with a mouse and test the slippery movement and melee combo.","Use right-click shooting and compare its backward recoil with forward melee propulsion.","Read the team’s Claude Code disclosure and human art, animation and audio credits.","Open the slick project folder in Godot 4.6, change one movement or gate rule, and test the first room, ammo and pause/restart controls.","Aidan “Botodo” Connolly and Evan Kurtz describe Claude Code helping diagnose problems and implement difficult core logic; they then touched and tweaked all code. They modeled, rigged, animated and designed the game themselves, using credited external audio. They explicitly state that generative AI was not used to create assets. No coding model version is supplied.",[102,468,469],"Procreate","Affinity","Godot 4.6 · GDScript · 3D",[102,468,469],[462,463,464,465],{"_65":460,"_31":436,"_23":185},{"_65":455,"_31":436,"_23":124,"_113":456},{"_65":450,"_31":451,"_183":184,"_113":452},{"_65":446,"_31":436,"_113":447},[180,478,182],"godot-engine","example:katana-kitsune-godot","katana-kitsune-godot","Katana Kitsune: Prototype","Choose a kitsune fighter and face yokai in an isometric action roguelike with katana combat, stamina, pickups and successive dungeon floors. The silent prototype supports local multiplayer, with additional party systems documented in the current source.","/examples/katana-kitsune-godot/",{"_25":480,"_27":481,"_29":482,"_169":554,"_159":255,"_155":172,"_151":548,"_164":555,"_9":556,"_136":557,"_125":558,"_38":559,"_109":560,"_97":561},[486,487,488,489,490,491,492,493,494,495,496,497,498,499,500,501,502,503,504,505,506],{"_61":27,"_74":481,"_63":27,"_98":-7},{"_61":170,"_74":482,"_63":29,"_98":-7},{"_61":71,"_65":167,"_74":554,"_63":169,"_98":152},{"_61":90,"_65":161,"_142":162,"_67":549,"_63":164,"_98":-7},{"_61":71,"_65":157,"_74":251,"_63":159,"_98":160},{"_61":71,"_65":153,"_74":154,"_63":155,"_98":156},{"_61":71,"_65":149,"_74":548,"_63":151,"_98":152},{"_61":90,"_65":141,"_142":143,"_67":543,"_63":9,"_98":-7},{"_61":62,"_65":137,"_67":539,"_63":136,"_98":-7},{"_61":71,"_65":134,"_74":135,"_63":136,"_98":-7},{"_61":71,"_65":132,"_74":457,"_63":125,"_98":-7},{"_61":62,"_65":126,"_67":535,"_63":125,"_98":-7},{"_61":71,"_65":123,"_74":124,"_63":125,"_98":-7},{"_61":62,"_65":117,"_67":531,"_63":38,"_98":-7},{"_61":71,"_65":115,"_74":116,"_63":38,"_98":-7},{"_61":62,"_65":107,"_67":526,"_63":109,"_98":-7},{"_61":62,"_65":95,"_67":516,"_63":97,"_98":-7},{"_61":90,"_63":91,"_65":92,"_67":514},{"_61":76,"_63":77,"_65":510,"_79":511,"_81":512,"_38":513,"_84":85,"_86":87,"_88":89},{"_61":71,"_63":72,"_65":73,"_74":217},{"_61":62,"_63":64,"_65":66,"_67":507},[508],{"_65":66,"_31":509},"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/9-K9/KatanaKitsune/bc9321eeaac727bbb5372a315ec58f68c96240ac/marketing/itch/05_attack.png","Creator-published combat screenshot from the silent Godot prototype.","/GameMap/assets/media/learning/katana-kitsune-godot.webp","The creator’s Katana Kitsune combat screenshot with an isometric courtyard, the party, enemies, health bars and minimap.","https://github.com/9-K9/KatanaKitsune/blob/bc9321eeaac727bbb5372a315ec58f68c96240ac/marketing/itch/05_attack.png",[94,515],"GitHub Copilot",[517,518,519,520,521],{"_65":94,"_31":106},{"_65":442,"_31":443},{"_65":524,"_31":525},{"_65":522,"_31":523},{"_65":102,"_31":103},"Meshy API","/resources/meshy/","PixelLab AI Agent Toolkit","/resources/pixellab/",[527],{"_65":528,"_31":529,"_113":530},"Read the creator’s AI production disclosure","https://9-k9.itch.io/katanakitsune","The author explicitly names Claude Code and GitHub Copilot alongside image, sprite and 3D asset tools, and links the primary complete source repository. The README verifies the Godot version and explains which finished assets are included.",[532],{"_65":450,"_31":533,"_113":534},"https://github.com/9-K9/KatanaKitsune","Godot 4.7 project with scenes, GDScript, Dialogic addon and finished sprite assets. The inspected tree contains about 383 MB of files; no top-level game license was found. The upstream Meshy/Blender/PixelOver authoring pipeline is separate, while its finished runtime sprites are committed. The current source contains newer party/asset changes than the reviewed hosted prototype.",[536],{"_65":537,"_31":529,"_113":538},"Play Katana Kitsune on itch.io","Silent HTML5 prototype with keyboard and gamepad support. Space confirms player/device choices; allow a clear press and release between setup steps. The browser build loaded and reached player/device selection in review; combat and a complete dungeon run were not exercised. The download is large: about 184 MB of game data plus 40 MB of WebAssembly.",[540],{"_65":541,"_31":542,"_113":-7},"Read the game and asset-pipeline documentation","https://github.com/9-K9/KatanaKitsune#readme",[544,545,546,547],"Open the itch prototype and choose one human player, then claim a keyboard and select a costume.","Read the creator’s AI disclosure and the repository’s character, combat and sprite-pipeline notes.","Open project.godot in Godot 4.7 using GL Compatibility; the finished sprites and game scenes are included.","Change one combat or spawn setting, then check the title-to-character-to-dungeon flow, damage and restart.","The creator identifies Claude Code, GitHub Copilot, GPT Image 2, PixelLab and Meshy among the production tools. The repository documents Meshy rigs and animation, Blender retargeting and PixelOver sprite exports. The exact coding models and division of code between assistants are not specified; generated NPC teammates are not the evidence for AI-assisted development.",[550,551,552,102,553],"GPT Image 2","PixelLab","Meshy","PixelOver","Godot 4.7 · GDScript · 2D / GL Compatibility",[550,551,552,102,553],[544,545,546,547],{"_65":541,"_31":542,"_23":185},{"_65":537,"_31":529,"_23":124,"_113":538},{"_65":450,"_31":533,"_183":184,"_113":534},{"_65":528,"_31":529,"_113":530},[180,478,562,563,182],"pixellab","meshy","resource:blender","resource","An open-sourc